## Answer

The coefficient matrix is $(a-b)I+bJ$, with eigenvalues $a-b$ (multiplicity $n-1$) and $a+(n-1)b$ (multiplicity one). Thus:

- only the zero solution if $a\ne b$ and $a+(n-1)b\ne0$;
- if $a=b$, the solutions satisfy $x_1+\cdots+x_n=0$;
- if $a+(n-1)b=0$, the solutions are $x=t(1,\ldots,1)^T$.
